# Adopt-First (discovery before scaffold)

Before inventing modules, services, or substantial new code, **search then decide**.  
Runbook (research-backed): `docs/CURSOR_ERP_SAAS_SETUP_GUIDE.md`  
Findings: `docs/plans/2026-08-02-cursor-oss-strategy-findings.md`

## Mandatory order (skip only for tiny in-file fixes)

1. **In-repo** — `docs/decisions/`, packages/apps, progressive memory (claude-mem / plans), and lane map (`rufler.yaml` / `AGENTS.md`).
2. **Skills** — `.cursor/skills/` → [skills.sh](https://skills.sh/) / `npx skills find` — license + exclusion check before install.
3. **MCP** — [awesome-mcp-servers](https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers); prefer read-only; do not mass-enable.
4. **Open source** — GitHub topics, [awesome-selfhosted](https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted) — **Integrate → Fork → Build**. Prefer MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD; **flag AGPL/GPL**.
5. **Only then invent** — thin adapters; one system of record; Discovery note in plan/PR.

## Decision shorthand

| Path | When |
|------|------|
| **Integrate** | Self-hostable OSS satellite or library; you own the adapter |
| **Fork** | Durable control of a permissive base; budget merge cost |
| **Build** | Differentiator, hard exclusions, or no OSS fit after honest search |

**No proprietary “Buy” recommendations** unless the user explicitly asks for commercial/SaaS options.

## Hard stops (GTR)

- No ZIMRA / FDMS / fiscalisation / payroll-tax skills, MCP, or modules.
- Bridge-First: no HTML5/WebView QR, printer, biometric, or GPS shortcuts.
- Do not rebase SoR onto ERPNext/Odoo mid-project.
- Do not auto-install every skill or MCP server.
- Do not dual-run Ruflo swarm orchestration and Cursor manager on one dirty tree.
